      <div type="clause" n="41">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 41</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.1-2"/> weofedþen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.17"/> manslaga weorðe oððon elles to swyðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.18"/> mánweorc gewyrce, þonne þolige he ægþer ge hades ge eðles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.19"/> ⁊ wræcnige, swa wide swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.20"/> papa him scrife, ⁊ dædbete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.21"/> georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Be gehadedu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gyf weofodðegen manslaga wyrðe oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.1"/> elles to swiðe mánweorc gewyrce, ðonne ðolie he ægðer ge hades ge éðles ⁊ wrécnige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.2"/>, swa wíde swa se papa him scrife, ⁊ dædbete georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="340" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif wefodþegen manslaga wyrðe oððe helles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.2-2"/> to swiðe manweorc geweorce, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þolige he ægðer ge hades ge eðeles ⁊ wræcnige, swa wide swa papa him scrife, ⁊ dætbete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.2-2"/> georne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis minister altaris hominem occidat aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.6"/> in aliis (uel malis) actibus supra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.7"/> modum differatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.8"/>, ordine simul et dignitate priuetur, et peregrinetur, sicut ei papa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.9"/> suus iniunget, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.10"/> opus emendet sedulo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si minister altaris homicidium fecerit aut aliquod magnum scelus, careat et ordine et liberalitate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.8-2"/> sua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.9-2"/> et uadat in exilium, secundum quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.10-2"/> papa sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_41.lnote.oe.11"/> constituerit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="41" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>Si minister altaris homicidium aut aliud criminale peccatum pat[ra]uerit, careat tam ordinibus quam dignitate delictumque corrigat uago exilio, sicut ei papa decreuerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="41" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="196" ed="#robertson"/>Be gehadedum mannum. Gyf weofodðegen manslaga wyrðe oððon<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_41.robnote.fn.5"/> elles to swiðe mánweorc gewyrce, ðonne ðolie he ægðer ge hades ge éðles, ⁊ wrécnige swa wíde swa se<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.robnote.fn.2"/> papa him scrife ⁊ dædbete georne.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="276" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf weofedþen manslaga weorðe oððon elles to swyðe manweorc gewyrce, þonne þolige he ægþer ge hades ge eðles, and wræcnige swa wide swa papa him scrife, and dædbete georne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="341" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von geweihten Männern. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.1"/> ein Altardiener<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.2"/> Todtschläger wird oder sonst zu arg Missethat verübt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.3"/>, dann verliere er beides, sowohl geistlichen Grad wie Heim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.4"/> [sammt bürgerlichem Rang] und pilgere elend verbannt, so weit wie der<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.5"/> Papst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_41.lnote.de.6"/> ihm zur Absolution auferlegen wird, und thue eifrig geistliche Busse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of men in orders. B) If a servant of the altar becomes a slayer or otherwise commits too grievous a misdeed, then let him lose both his orders and his homeland [with his civil rank], and go into exile on pilgrimage as far as the Pope prescribes for him, and do eager penance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_41.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="197" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning men in holy orders. If a minister of the altar<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_41.robnote.n.2"/> commits homicide or perpetrates any other great crime, he shall be deprived of his ecclesiastical office and banished, and shall travel as a pilgrim as far as the Pope appoints for him, and zealously make amends.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_41.whinote.n.3"/><pb n="468" ed="#whitelock"/>If a minister of the altar becomes a homicide or otherwise commits too grave a crime, he is then to forfeit both his ecclesiastical orders and his native land, and to go on a pilgrimage as far as the pope may prescribe for him, and zealously to make atonement.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="277" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If a minister at the altar commits murder or any other serious crime, then he shall forfeit both his office and his native land, and he must go on a pilgrimage as far as the pope prescribes for him, and fervently do penance.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="341"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_26">VIII Atr 26</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 26</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_26">VIII Atr 26</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 41: VIII Atr 26</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="468"><label>almost exactly as</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_26">VIII Atr 26</ref> <quote>Almost exactly as in VIII Ethelred, 26.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 26.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 341, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
